        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: North Koʻolaupoko, Kāneʻohe, Oʻahu, Hawaii, United States\n- Organizations: City & County of Honolulu\n- Concepts: Hawaiian place-name origins, ancient Hawaiian story\n\nFacts:\n- North Koʻolaupoko is an area in the City & County of Honolulu in Hawaii, United States, on the island of Oʻahu.\n- An ancient Hawaiian story says that a local woman compared her husband's cruelty to the sharp edge of cutting bamboo.\n- The place name Kāneʻohe was thus explained as meaning \"Bamboo man\" in that story.",
